<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Tangents: tangent parallel to a given line (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The graph shows the curve \( y = {@fx@} \) (blue) and the line \( y = {@gl@} \) (dashed green).</p>
[[jsxgraph width="440px" height="400px"]]
var p = {#pq#}, q = {#qq#}, r = {#rq#};
var m = {#mt#}, k = {#k0#}, a = {#aa#};
function f(x){ return (p*x + q)*x + r; }
function g(x){ return m*x + k; }
var x0 = Math.min(a, 0) - 4, x1 = Math.max(a, 0) + 4;
var lo = Infinity, hi = -Infinity;
for (var s = x0; s <= x1 + 1e-9; s += 0.05) { var v = f(s); lo = Math.min(lo, v); hi = Math.max(hi, v); }
lo = Math.max(lo, f(a) - 14); hi = Math.min(hi, f(a) + 14);
var pad = 0.1*(hi - lo) + 1;
var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [x0, hi + pad, x1, lo - pad],
    axis: true, showCopyright: false, showNavigation: false,
    pan: {enabled:false}, zoom: {enabled:false}
});
board.create('functiongraph', [f, x0, x1], {strokeColor:'#1565c0', strokeWidth:2, highlight:false});
board.create('functiongraph', [g, x0, x1], {strokeColor:'#2e7d32', strokeWidth:2, dash:2, highlight:false});
[[/jsxgraph]]
<p>There is exactly one tangent to the curve that is <strong>parallel</strong> to the dashed line.</p>
<p>(a) Find the coordinates of the point where this tangent touches the curve.</p>
<div>\( x = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div>\( y = \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(b) Find the equation of the tangent.</p>
<div>\( y = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Parallel lines have the <strong>same gradient</strong>, so the tangent must have gradient \( {@mt@} \), the gradient of \( y = {@gl@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(a)</strong> The curve has gradient \( f'(x) = {@dfx@} \). Set it equal to \( {@mt@} \):</p>
\[ {@dfx@} = {@mt@} \quad\Longrightarrow\quad x = {@aa@}. \]
<p>Then \( f({@aa@}) = {@fa@} \), so the point of tangency is \( ({@aa@},\ {@fa@}) \).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> The tangent has gradient \( {@mt@} \) and passes through \( ({@aa@},\ {@fa@}) \):</p>
\[ y = {@mt@}\left(x - ({@aa@})\right) + ({@fa@}) = {@tl@}. \]
<p>It has the same gradient as \( y = {@gl@} \) but a different intercept, so the two lines are parallel and distinct.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
